<section aria-labelledby="meaning-in-context"><h2 id="meaning-in-context">One word, different contexts · 一字多義</h2>
<details class="reading-topic"><summary>bill · payment or legislation?</summary><div class="reading-topic-body">
<p><strong>Payment:</strong> an electricity / phone / gas bill; a bill for repairs; run up a huge bill; ask for the bill; foot the bill (= pay it).</p>
<p class="reading-example">Could we have the bill, please? The company will foot the bill for the repairs.<span class="reading-translation" lang="zh-Hant">可以幫我們結帳嗎？公司會支付這次維修的費用。</span></p>
<p><strong>Legislation:</strong> amend a bill; pass a bill; throw out a bill (= reject it). A bill becomes law through the applicable lawmaking process.</p><p class="reading-translation" lang="zh-Hant"><strong>帳單、付費：</strong>electricity bill 電費帳單；run up a huge bill 累積大筆費用；ask for the bill 請店家結帳；foot the bill 支付費用。<br><strong>法案：</strong>amend a bill 修訂法案；pass a bill 通過法案；throw out a bill 否決法案。法案須完成適用的立法程序才成為法律。</p>
<p class="reading-example">The committee amended the bill before the vote.<span class="reading-translation" lang="zh-Hant">委員會在表決前修訂了法案。</span></p>
</div></details>
<details class="reading-topic"><summary>pilot · person, trial, or guidance?</summary><div class="reading-topic-body">
<p><strong>A person:</strong> an aircraft pilot or a harbor pilot. <strong>A trial:</strong> a pilot episode, pilot project, or pilot program.</p>
<p><strong>As a verb:</strong> pilot an aircraft; pilot a new service in a selected market; <strong>pilot a bill through parliament</strong> (= guide it through the process).</p>
<p>A <strong>pilot light</strong> is a small gas flame. For a product trial, use “pilot a product in a market”; “pilot a product to” is not a general fixed pattern.</p><p class="reading-translation" lang="zh-Hant"><strong>人物：</strong>aircraft pilot 飛行員；harbor pilot 港口引水人。<br><strong>試辦：</strong>pilot episode 試播集；pilot program 試辦計畫。作動詞時，pilot a service 指試辦服務；pilot a bill through parliament 指「引導、推動法案通過議會」，強調協助法案完成審議程序；單純說「通過法案」通常用 <strong>pass a bill</strong>。<br><strong>pilot light</strong> 是常明的引火火焰。試行產品可用 pilot a product <strong>in</strong> a market，不把「pilot a product to」當作固定搭配背誦。</p>
</div></details>
<details class="reading-topic"><summary>vintage · a period, wine, or quality?</summary><div class="reading-topic-body">
<p><strong>Vintage champagne / port / claret</strong> relates to wine from a specified year or harvest. As a noun, a vintage can mean that year or the wine produced from it.</p>
<p><strong>Vintage clothing / cars</strong> refers to an earlier period, often with a suggestion of lasting value. “Vintage” does not simply mean “best” in every context. Figuratively, “a vintage performance” can mean a notably good, characteristic one.</p>
<p>A phrase such as <strong>a vintage of researchers</strong> can refer to a group from the same period; “generation” or “cohort” is more transparent in ordinary study notes.</p><p class="reading-translation" lang="zh-Hant"><strong>酒：</strong>指特定年份釀製的酒，或該酒的釀造年份。<br><strong>衣物、汽車：</strong>指具有年代特色、常帶有收藏價值的物品，不是一律翻成「最好的」。a vintage performance 可引申為「表現出色、盡顯典型風格的一次演出」。<br>用於一批人或物時，可表示「同一時期的」；一般筆記用 generation（世代）或 cohort（同期群體）較清楚。</p>
</div></details>
